  "findings": [
    "OER articles 11.3–11.4 confirm ten year-one courses, eight compulsory year-two courses and two restricted year-two choices, one in each of periods 5 and 6. All carry 6 EC. Article 12.1 establishes at least 30 EC in the third-year autumn.",
    "Article 9.1 requires Methodology 2 or an older equivalent before Methodology 3. It identifies Methodology 5 with its course code still unknown and requires Methodology 3 or the old Epidemiology and Biostatistics II. The 42 EC placement gate is listed under students starting before 2025–2026.",
    "The same OER lists the currently offered third-year 6 EC Epidemiology and Biostatistics III and 18 EC placement. The older-cohort progression is explicit, and the revised Methodology 5, professional module, placement and thesis cannot be fully weighted or sequenced from the current guide. The faculty page describes the three-month placement and thesis and names the professional course without credits. Subsequent annual-guide requests returned 404. The 2025–2026 guide is earlier and cannot fill the missing later-year ledger."
  ],
